WEBVTT

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.287
This section will focus on describing
the problem-solving framework and discussing

00:00:05.327 --> 00:00:09.870
problem-solving strategies that can
be used to better cope with tinnitus.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:14.095
As previously mentioned,
we are representing these particular

00:00:14.135 --> 00:00:18.010
forms of coping strategies
by the Problem Solving Toolbox.

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:23.030
In the first part of this section,
we will teach you a problem-solving framework.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:26.270
This has been researched
by psychologists for years.

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.300
Please see the reference
section if you want

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.330
more details about two
books on this topic.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:38.070
Typically, problem-solving
is taught in a five-step process.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:42.622
But before starting the process,
you must think about the issue or problem

00:00:42.662 --> 00:00:46.733
causing you stress to make sure
that you should be using problem-solving

00:00:46.773 --> 00:00:50.310
to change the particular form
of stress that you are experiencing.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.901
Remember to ask the can-do questions

00:00:52.941 --> 00:00:56.810
to determine whether you
can change a situation.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:01.750
First, what can I do
to eliminate the problem?

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:07.070
Second, what can someone else
do to eliminate the problem?

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.598
After determining
that an issue is changeable,

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:17.020
then begin the following problem-solving
process that involves five steps.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:23.824
These five steps are creating options,
listing possible outcomes for each option,

00:01:23.864 --> 00:01:28.792
sorting through your options,
choosing and implementing one option,

00:01:28.832 --> 00:01:33.740
and then finally evaluating
the effectiveness of that option.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:38.880
The following two slides will give more
information about each of the steps.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.440
First, create options.

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:46.480
Think about possible ways
of changing the stress.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.212
This can be done by your own brainstorming

00:01:49.252 --> 00:01:52.940
or by talking with someone
else about the ideas.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:56.991
It is usually helpful to get
the full range of options,

00:01:57.031 --> 00:02:00.340
including some humorous
or bizarre solutions.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:06.520
This step often involves seeking out
information and thinking about your options.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.020
Second, list possible
outcomes of each option.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.880
Think about the pluses
and minuses of each option.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:19.920
Think about what may happen if
you use a particular option.

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:25.407
Some people find it useful to write out
pros and cons of choices on a piece of paper

00:02:25.447 --> 00:02:31.440
by making two columns and listing out
the possible value or drawback of each option.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.740
Third, sort your options.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:39.938
Now put the listing in an order
with the options that you most prefer

00:02:39.978 --> 00:02:45.000
at the top and the ones that you least
prefer at the bottom of the list.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:48.696
Which choice has the least
minuses or drawbacks

00:02:48.736 --> 00:02:52.120
or cons or possible negative outcomes?

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:56.060
Fourth, choose one option.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.500
Select one option and try it out.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:02.220
Fifth, evaluate your choice.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:04.480
How did the approach work?

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.900
Do you want to try something else?

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:12.340
If so, choose another approach,
implement it, and evaluate the outcome.

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:16.395
Now we will run through
an exercise related to tinnitus

00:03:16.435 --> 00:03:19.760
to help you practice
the problem solving framework.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:23.305
It is important to remember
that you will probably not have

00:03:23.345 --> 00:03:26.520
the same answers that we list
in the following exercise.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:32.180
That is okay because each person appraises
a stressful situation differently.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:38.260
What matters here is how you view
a situation and what works well for you.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:42.170
Here's the problem.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:47.630
Your tinnitus often is bothersome to you
at night and you do not sleep well.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:49.311
You have asked for sleep medication,

00:03:49.351 --> 00:03:52.830
but your physician will not
prescribe a sleep medication to you.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:55.647
This is because your doctor
thinks that you should find

00:03:55.687 --> 00:03:58.950
ways to sleep naturally
and get used to your tinnitus.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.539
Your doctor also thinks
you will become addicted

00:04:01.579 --> 00:04:05.590
to the sleep medication if
it is prescribed to you now.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:11.930
Your first step is to list
your options to solve this problem.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:16.210
Remember that this involves brainstorming
about some possible actions.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:19.750
For instance, you might

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:22.410
1. Get a second opinion,

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:26.730
2. Go to the pharmacy and buy
an over-the-counter sedative,

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:29.710
3. Negotiate with your doctor,

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:33.970
4. Enroll in a clinical
trial for sleeping problems,

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:39.290
5. Get an appointment with an audiologist
who specializes in tinnitus, or

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:43.450
6. You can add your own thoughts
to this list of possible options.

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:49.623
Your second step is to list possible outcomes,
that is, write out the possible

00:04:49.663 --> 00:04:54.690
pros and cons or positive or negative
consequences of each option.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.450
Option 1.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:58.670
Negotiate with your doctor.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.048
The pro is you might change your doctor's

00:05:01.088 --> 00:05:04.070
mind about tinnitus
and get the medication.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:08.066
The cons are this will require
patience to wait for an appointment

00:05:08.106 --> 00:05:11.930
and your doctor may still refuse
to give you what you want.

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:13.830
Option 2.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:15.650
Get a second opinion.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:20.230
The pro is you might get a different
answer and get the medication.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:24.100
The cons are this will require
patience to wait for your appointment

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:28.170
and you might get the same
refusal from the second doctor.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:30.250
Option 3.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:34.010
Go to the pharmacy and buy
an over-the-counter sedative.

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:36.610
The pro is this can be done today.

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:42.150
The cons are this over-the-counter
sedative may not help you sleep.

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:46.150
Option 4.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:49.250
Enroll in a clinical trial
for sleeping problems.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:54.230
The pro is the researchers may help
you figure out how to sleep better.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:58.317
The cons are the researchers may
not understand your form of tinnitus

00:05:58.357 --> 00:06:02.697
or if you were assigned to the control
group, you might have to wait

00:06:02.737 --> 00:06:07.330
a while for the clinical trial to conclude
before receiving the treatment.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.050
Option 5.

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:13.770
Get an appointment with an audiologist
who specializes in tinnitus.

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:18.698
The pro is you might get ideas about how
to handle tinnitus symptoms at night.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:23.390
The con is your audiologist cannot
give you any prescription medication.
